Thanks @geco for sharing your persistence plugin! It's great to see the MemPalace integration evolving.

I wanted to share another approach that complements the persistence work - **automatic Memory Injection with Wake-up Context** using the `experimental.chat.messages.transform` hook.

While your plugin handles the *write* side (saving conversations), I've been experimenting with the *read* side - automatically injecting relevant memories and wake-up context **before** the AI processes each message, without relying on model discipline to search MemPalace.

## Key Implementation

The core mechanism uses `experimental.chat.messages.transform` to intercept and augment user messages:

```javascript
"experimental.chat.messages.transform": async (_input, output) => {
  if (!output?.messages?.length) return output
  const lastUser = [...output.messages].reverse().find(m => m.info?.role === "user")
  if (!lastUser) return output

  // 1. Wake-up: Inject L0+L1 context on first message
  if (!wakeupDone) {
    wakeupDone = true
    const ctx = wakeup()  // Calls `mempalace wake-up`
    if (ctx) {
      lastUser.parts.push({
        id: `mp-wakeup-${Date.now()}`,
        type: "text",
        synthetic: true,
        text: `[MemPalace Context]\n${ctx}\n[/MemPalace Context]`
      })
    }
  }

  // 2. Recall: Search and inject relevant memories
  const query = textFromParts(lastUser.parts, true)
  const memories = search(query)  // Similarity search with budget control
  if (memories) {
    lastUser.parts.push({
      id: `mp-recall-${Date.now()}`,
      type: "text",
      synthetic: true,
      text: `[MemPalace Recall]\n${memories}\n[/MemPalace Recall]`
    })
  }

  return output
}
```

## Benefits

1. **Guaranteed Recall** - Doesn't depend on model following AGENTS.md instructions (which smaller models skip ~60% of the time)
2. **Wake-up Context** - Provides L0+L1 identity/project context automatically, similar to AAAK pattern
3. **Token Efficient** - Uses similarity thresholds (MIN_SIMILARITY=0.20) and character budgets (MAX_INJECT_CHARS=900)
4. **Zero Configuration** - No need for separate AGENTS.md or identity.txt files

## Storage Side

For the persistence side, maybe consider following:
```javascript
function store(content) {
  // Write to temp file
  const tempFile = `/tmp/mp-store-${Date.now()}.txt`
  writeFileSync(tempFile, content)

  // Call mempalace mine
  execSync(`mempalace mine ${tempFile} --mode convos`)

  // Cleanup
  unlinkSync(tempFile)
}
```
